# M7 - e2e test gate for the swarm simulation (DONE)

## Root cause fixed
The gate failed on the mandatory pre-step: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity`.
`manus-parity` had advanced since the earlier merge, so `git merge manus-parity`
re-conflicted. The only conflict was `package.json`: this branch added
`"test:mirofish"` and `manus-parity` added `"test:coding-eval"`. Resolved by
keeping BOTH scripts (commit a32783a). No other files conflicted; working tree clean.

## What M7 ships (commit ca4411f)
- `src/tools/mirofish/types.ts` - public pipeline contract: `ModelCaller` (injectable,
  the only model boundary), `LocaleProfile`, `Persona`, `SimulationEvent`,
  `RoundMetrics`, `SwarmReport`, `PipelineResult`, `MirofishChatRequest`,
  `MirofishPipelineUnavailableError`.
- `src/tools/mirofish/pipeline.ts` - `runMirofishPipeline` (seed -> simulate ->
  report) and `runMirofishChat` (the entry point shared with the `mirofish_chat`
  tool), plus the per-stage capability check `mirofishPipelineReady()`.
- `src/tools/mirofish/__tests__/nutrio-e2e.test.ts` - the e2e gate. A deterministic
  fake `ModelCaller` whose replies depend on prompt content (locale keywords drive
  currency/dialect; the active price drives purchase intent), so price and location
  genuinely change outcomes. Four scenarios:
  1. Doha/QAR/Arabic-Gulf: report mentions Nutrio, keto and both prices; personas use QAR.
  2. Price sensitivity 1200 / 1450 / 99999 -> three distinct purchase-intent metrics.
  3. Location: London -> GBP/English and a report that differs from Doha; unset
     location -> inferred from the brief.
  4. Static gate: scans `src/tools/mirofish*` for hard-coded result numbers, fake
     personas (`Developer`/`SecurityAuditor`/...), `readdirSync` folder scanning and
     `approval_rate_*` keys, and fails if any are found.
- `src/tools/mirofish/__tests__/fixtures/nutrio-briefs.ts` - Nutrio / نتريو meal
  subscription brief (price QAR 1200 -> 1450, new keto plan) with Doha, London and
  unset-location variants plus `withPrice`.
- `package.json` - added `"test:mirofish"`.

## Capability guard (per the task spec)
The pipeline stages (seed/simulate/report) are not implemented on manus-parity, so
`mirofishPipelineReady()` returns false and every scenario skips via `skip: !ready`
(no `test.todo`). The suite prints which checks are pending and stays green. A later
stage task flips its own capability flag in `pipeline.ts` and the matching assertions
turn on automatically.

## Gates (all pass on the merged branch)
- `npx tsc --noEmit` -> exit 0
- `npm run build:server` -> exit 0
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)` -> exit 0
- `npm run test:mirofish` -> exit 0 (4 scenarios SKIP via capability guard, prints pending list)
- `node --import tsx --test src/tools/mirofish/__tests__/nutrio-e2e.test.ts` -> exit 0

## Notes
- The legacy fake `src/tools/mirofish.ts` (mirofish_chat tool + /api/mirofish routes)
  is intentionally left in place for now; the static gate will start failing on it once
  the capability flag flips, which is the intended signal for the stage tasks.
- No files outside the worktree were touched; no secrets; no pushes; no reset --hard.
